    "content": "Vaccinations are safe, effective tools using the body's natural defenses to build resistance to infections, preventing over 30 dangerous diseases. Essential for all ages, they protect against illnesses like COVID-19, influenza, measles, and HPV, with routine schedules recommended for infants, children, and adults to maintain immunity. Key Vaccination Information for 2026: Childhood & Adult Vaccines: Recommended vaccines include DTaP/Tdap (pertussis), MMR (measles, mumps, rubella), HPV, Hepatitis A/B, Polio, and Pneumococcal. RSV Protection: Vaccination against RSV is recommended for older adults (aged 60+) to prevent severe respiratory illness. Flu and COVID-19: Yearly influenza vaccines and updated 2025-26 COVID-19 shots are advised for individuals aged 6 months and older. Vaccine Access: Vaccines are available at health departments, doctor offices, and pharmacies (e.g., CVS MinuteClinic). CVS MinuteClinic Vaccine Trends: While vaccines are highly effective, a 2025 analysis found declining childhood vaccination rates in over 77% of U.S. counties, prompting renewed emphasis on staying up to date. Finding Vaccination Records: You can order your immunization records, or your children's, through regional registries like Maryland MyIR Mobile or by contacting your state's health department. Maryland MyIR Mobile",
